{
  "content": {
    "body": "The sanctioned mutation gateway. All output is JSON on stdout; failures\nprint `{\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"…\"}` and exit 1 — and the error text\nteaches the fix. Without `--project <root>` the CLI walks up from the\ncwd to the dir containing `.pebbles/`. Pebble paths may be\nproject-relative (\"models/user.pebble\") or include \".pebbles/\"; a\nmissing extension self-heals. There is deliberately NO delete — mark\nthings `deprecated`; removal is a human decision in the app.\n\n## READ\n\n- `sections` — the section keys.\n- `list <section>` — tree of one section (titles, status, health).\n  Example: `pebbles-cli list models`\n- `get <path>` — one pebble in full.\n  Example: `pebbles-cli get models/user.pebble`\n- `query [--section S] [--status X] [--unit-status X] [--type T]\n  [--text SUBSTR]` — find pebbles across the graph; flags AND together.\n  `--unit-status` matches at ITEM/FIELD/NODE level and returns the\n  matching units in each row.\n  Examples: `pebbles-cli query --status broken` ·\n  `pebbles-cli query --unit-status planned --section models` ·\n  `pebbles-cli query --text webhook`\n- `refs <path>` — a pebble's connections BOTH ways: outgoing refs\n  (pebble- and unit-level) + codeLinks, and every pebble/unit that\n  references it (backlinks, incl. subprocess/typeRef/refKey edges).\n  Example: `pebbles-cli refs models/user.pebble`\n- `validate <path>` — structural check; returns valid:true or the\n  exact error.\n- `arrange <path>` — auto-lay-out a workflow's node positions with the\n  app's layout engine (straight spine, 2-way splits peel right,\n  collision-free); locked nodes kept, --only-unpositioned moves just\n  origin nodes. Agents should run this instead of placing nodes by hand.\n- `onboard` — add/refresh the marker-guarded Pebbles briefing in\n  CLAUDE.md + AGENTS.md (creates AGENTS.md when neither exists).\n\n## CODE GRAPH (see the code-map knowledge doc)\n\n- `map [--max N] [--fresh]` — (re)build + save the dependency graph.\n- `map-symbol <name> [--kind K]` — where a symbol is DEFINED\n  (file:line:kind). Example: `pebbles-cli map-symbol User --kind class`\n- `map-file <path>` — a file's symbols + imports + imported-by + calls.\n- `map-search <term> [--max N]` — files/symbols ranked by importance.\n- `map-neighbors <path> [--in|--out] [--depth N]` — dependency closure.\n- `map-callers <symbol>` — every call site, calling function attributed.\n\n## WRITE (validated + atomic — the ONLY way spec changes)\n\n- `create <section> --title T [--kind K] [--dir SUB] [--content JSON]`\n  Filename auto-kebabs from the title. Returns `{ok, path, id,\n  droppedRefs}`.\n  Example: `pebbles-cli create models --title \"Order\" --content\n  '{\"kind\":\"fields\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"order_id\",\"type\":\"integer\",\n  \"required\":true,\"status\":\"implemented\",\"description\":\"PK\",\n  \"primaryKey\":true}]}'`\n- `update <path> --patch JSON` — merges top-level keys; `content` is\n  replaced WHOLE (send the full object). id/version/createdAt are\n  immutable. Units matched by id (or by name when the patch has no id)\n  inherit their previous id, status and description when omitted —\n  explicit values always win. Returns `{ok, path, droppedRefs}`.\n- `set-status <path> <status> [--unit ID]` — pebble- or unit-level;\n  validated against the status vocabulary.\n  Example: `pebbles-cli set-status models/user.pebble verified --unit f1`\n- `add-item <path> --text T [--status S] [--description D]` — append a\n  checklist entry.\n- `add-finding <target> --title T [--unit ID] [--category C]\n  [--severity S] [--body MARKDOWN] [--supersedes <finding-path>]` — creates\n  a DATED report in findings/ and cross-links BOTH ways (pebble +\n  unit). APPEND-ONLY: never update/delete a finding — supersede it.\n  `--body` is full markdown: sections are convention (## Observation,\n  ## Evidence, ## Impact, ## Root cause, ## Solution, ## Solution steps)\n  but not enforced — the author owns the structure.\n  Categories: bug · verified-working · spec-violation · security ·\n  performance · regression · tech-debt · ux · data · research ·\n  decision · assumption · measurement · incomplete · other.\n  Disposition at birth (immutable): open/resolved/info — derived from\n  the category, overridable with --disposition.\n  Example: `pebbles-cli add-finding models/user.pebble --title \"Email\n  uniqueness verified\" --category verified-working --body \"## Observation\\n\\nEmail field checked for uniqueness\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- users table migration L42\\n- UserTest::test_unique_email passes\"`\n- `link-code <pebble> --file <rel> [--symbol S] [--line N] [--note X]`\n  — bind spec to an implementing file (refuses files that don't exist;\n  absolute in-project paths normalize to relative).\n- `unlink-code <pebble> --id <linkId>` — remove one codeLink.\n\n## Enforced at write time\n\n1. FIELD COMPLETENESS: fields content is REJECTED when any field lacks\n   a description (what it's for, from the code) or a status.\n2. REFERENCE INTEGRITY: refs/typeRef/refKey/subprocess resolving to\n   nothing are DROPPED (never stored) and reported in droppedRefs.\n3. FK AUTO-WIRING: refKey may name the target field —\n   `{\"path\":\"models/user.pebble\",\"field\":\"user_id\"}` — the CLI\n   resolves the field id, fills pebbleId/label, and adds the graph refs\n   on both the field and the pebble (visible in Properties→Reference).\n4. STATUS VOCABULARY: set-status rejects unknown statuses and lists the\n   allowed ones.\n5. On a DB model, `required: true` means NOT NULL (the app shows it\n   inverted as \"Nullable\"); record real defaults in `default`.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
